{
    "info": {
        "_postman_id": "b1c2d3e4-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
        "name": "JMC Test API",
        "description": "Postman collection for the JMC Test Laravel API.\n\nAuthentication is session-based (Laravel Sanctum stateful API). There is no bearer token issued by /auth/login. To authenticate:\n\n1. Run `Auth > Get CSRF Cookie` (primes the XSRF-TOKEN cookie).\n2. Run `Auth > Login` (session cookie is stored in Postman's cookie jar).\n3. Protected requests then reuse the session cookie automatically.\n\nThe collection pre-request script adds the required `Referer`/`Origin` headers (stateful domain detection) and, for mutating requests, the `X-XSRF-TOKEN` header. Set the `token` environment variable only if you manually issue a Sanctum personal access token.",
        "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
    },
    "auth": {
        "type": "noauth"
    },
    "event": [
        {
            "listen": "prerequest",
            "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                    "const origin = pm.environment.get('stateful_origin') || pm.environment.get('base_url') || 'http://localhost:8000';",
                    "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Referer', value: origin });",
                    "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Origin', value: origin });",
                    "if (!pm.request.headers.has('Accept')) {",
                    "    pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Accept', value: 'application/json' });",
                    "}",
                    "",
                    "// Optional: manual Sanctum personal access token.",
                    "const bearer = pm.environment.get('token');",
                    "if (bearer) {",
                    "    pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Authorization', value: 'Bearer ' + bearer });",
                    "}",
                    "",
                    "// CSRF token required for stateful mutating requests.",
                    "const xsrf = pm.environment.get('xsrf_token');",
                    "if (xsrf && ['POST', 'PUT', 'PATCH', 'DELETE'].includes(pm.request.method)) {",
                    "    pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'X-XSRF-TOKEN', value: xsrf });",
                    "}"
                ]
            }
        }
    ],
    "item": [
        {
            "name": "Get Sanctum CSRF Cookie",
            "event": [
                {
                    "listen": "test",
                    "script": {
                        "type": "text/javascript",
                        "exec": [
                            "const xsrf = pm.cookies.get('XSRF-TOKEN');",
                            "if (xsrf) {",
                            "    pm.environment.set('xsrf_token', decodeURIComponent(xsrf));",
                            "    console.log('XSRF token stored.');",
                            "} else {",
                            "    console.warn('XSRF-TOKEN cookie not found. Check the CSRF endpoint and cookie domain.');",
                            "}"
                        ]
                    }
                }
            ],
            "request": {
                "auth": {
                    "type": "noauth"
                },
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [
                    {
                        "key": "Accept",
                        "value": "application/json"
                    }
                ],
                "url": {
                    "raw": "{{base_url}}/sanctum/csrf-cookie",
                    "host": [
                        "{{base_url}}"
                    ],
                    "path": [
                        "sanctum",
                        "csrf-cookie"
                    ]
                },
                "description": "Built-in Laravel Sanctum CSRF cookie endpoint. Run this before any stateful mutating request (e.g. Login). The test script stores the XSRF-TOKEN cookie in the `xsrf_token` environment variable."
            },
            "response": []
        },
